WARNING:BLOCK_COMMENT_STYLE: Block comments should align the * on each line
#49: FILE: kernel/locking/lockdep.c:72:
+/*
+* Queue rwlock only allows read-after-read recursion of the same lock class

The comment style is incorrect.  The preferred style for multi-
line comments is::

  /*
  * This is the preferred style
  * for multi line comments.
  */

The networking comment style is a bit different, with the first line
not empty like the former::

  /* This is the preferred comment style
  * for files in net/ and drivers/net/
  */

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#commenting

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'read == 2'
#65: FILE: kernel/locking/lockdep.c:1783:
+		if ((read == 2) && prev->read && allow_recursive_read)

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

